    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d864">

                <pb facs="1656" n="1616" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1616"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/8–1754: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 864<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                        Jordan</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d864-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-08-18T19:24:00-04:00">August 18, 1954—7:24
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. In light Dayan’s willingness urge
                    Israel participation in meeting HKJ and Israel
                    commanders Jerusalem sector late August (Deptel 67 to Tel Aviv<anchor n="2" xml:id="d864-f2"/> and Tel Aviv
                    173 to Dept<anchor n="3" xml:id="d864-f3"/>) and in view statement last para
                    Jerusalem’s 45 to Dept.,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d864-f4"/> request Amman’s and Tel
                    Aviv’s views as to practicability their approaching governments soonest to urge
                    such meeting. Should this approach be made without awaiting definitive result
                    efforts arrange meeting Gaza? <pb facs="1657" n="1617" xml:id="pg1617"/> Such an
                    approach would be along lines final para Deptel 205 to Cairo<anchor n="5" xml:id="d864-f5"/> with emphasis
                    on limited nature agenda.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d864-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d864-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also priority to Tel Aviv, Jerusalem, and Cairo; sent by pouch to Beirut,
                    London, and Damascus.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d864-f2" n="2" xml:id="d864-f2-content">
                <p>Printed as telegram 38 to Amman, <ref target="#d853">Document 853</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d864-f3" n="3" xml:id="d864-f3-content">
                <p>In telegram 173 from Tel Aviv, Aug. 17, Russell reported that he had raised with Eytan the possibility of reactivating,
                    improving, and extending the local commanders’ meetings. Eytan said he would prefer to postpone
                    discussion until Dayan returned from
                    Washington later in the week. (684A.85/8–1754)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d864-f4" n="4" xml:id="d864-f4-content">
                <p>In the last paragraph of telegram 45 from Jerusalem, Aug. 16, Cole reported that he had sounded out the
                    senior Arab Legion officer in the Jerusalem area about local commanders’
                    meetings. The officer’s opinion was that such meetings were useful and could
                    presumably be renewed whenever the Israelis signified a desire to do so.
                    (684A.85/8–1654)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d864-f5" n="5" xml:id="d864-f5-content">
                <p>Printed as telegram 38 to Amman, <ref target="#d853">Document 853</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
